{"acceptedClaimRefs":[{"assessmentDigest":"sha256:1c1de02aa4c671e39457c3c08845c2d41b95877d675814f6c36e848f9b03ebd2","claimKey":"bssc-sum-capacity/two-letter-marton-marginal-correlation-pruning","judgmentId":"sha256:dc34c24c1066faf7f4d68fd8ba8fd051664ccdbc4e8ce14dcd230729dc69240e","transactionId":"9bb22afe5abd3e1d9f419c1717bd61bb33a958ff"}],"acceptedClaims":[{"claimKey":"bssc-sum-capacity/two-letter-marton-marginal-correlation-pruning","dependencyTransactionIds":["33a5944dca980bf94cc869c6c7dee2d04385ff58","88a1004f309460f3ec1cacdae88d30f88559f9bc"],"statement":"For the governed half-skew BSSC product channel P^{otimes 2}, let M be the unnormalized finite-auxiliary Marton sum value of any law (W,U,V)-X_1X_2-(Y^2,Z^2), let q_i=Pr[X_i=1], Q=q_1+q_2, let C_out=I(Y_1;Y_2)+I(Z_1;Z_2), and let c_in=P(X_1X_2=11)-q_1q_2. Canonical transaction 33a5944dca980bf94cc869c6c7dee2d04385ff58 supplies the two pre-averaging Marton-to-input rows and their universal average M <= G(P_{X_1X_2})+2r, while canonical transaction 88a1004f309460f3ec1cacdae88d30f88559f9bc supplies the exact directed threshold T=2L_RTD. The exact identity G=F(q_1)+F(q_2)-C_out/2 and the coordinatewise concave row envelopes imply that M>T forces q_1,q_2 in (3/8,5/8), hence in (7/20,13/20), together with 17/20<Q<23/20, C_out<7/160=0.04375<0.044 bits, and |c_in|<7/40. On the reflected/transposed family P(00)=P(11)=alpha and P(01)=P(10)=1/2-alpha, a gain additionally forces 1/8<alpha<5/13. These are necessary conditions only; they do not establish a two-letter gain, rule one out, or give a capacity converse."}],"evidenceChunkDigests":["sha256:0a1716c89d079f622be5fef00e03251f5b300b5692275f529cb49a74caae574d","sha256:25a8cbc3b85fdacb4df9d8e92fd57f6468ba3060c56c94a5eebc35a5403d28a9","sha256:9764fcc6d169eaa82f04d483f6dec405c8df5eff3f9c94bcee3dd46a1ee40b69","sha256:fa482fa6cd2074e0ac5752bc676356f4af4a759392e2c23533422eae4ed4254e"],"evidenceManifest":{"chunkSizeBytes":65536,"contributionPath":"problems/bssc-sum-capacity/con